s Angeles Times", "username": "latimes"}, "content": "Surge in ICE raids is aimed at discouraging voter turnout, immigration advocates say", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 63}, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 17, "created": 1792206882000, "id": "2111294805548601772", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1461071086020435968/yt0TZ7ut_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Sean Davis", "username": "seanmdav"}, "content": "So illegals are voting. Good to know.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 1584}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVjYVWjB", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 9, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "peace", "id": 8890599, "raw_content": "", "author": "5DchessWatch", "created": 1792243205094, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Steve56775", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.washingtonexaminer.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/policy/defense/4768311/tiny-nuclear-bomb-trump-moab-iran/#google_vignette", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Trump considers MOABing Pickaxe Mountain.\u2e3bWhy not drop 3?", "last_comment_created": 1792245772891, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 3, "score_up": 9, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "The largest nonnuclear bomb in the U.S. arsenal, nicknamed the \"mother of all bombs,\" is designed to explode above ground.", "large_image": "PW6iKOS3rIypGFxD.png", "title": "'Like a tiny nuclear bomb': Trump details proposed heavy ordnance against Iran"}, "post_flair_text": "\u262a\ufe0f\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u262a\ufe0f", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVjYUycy", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 21, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "stable", "id": 8890390, "raw_content": "Campus early-voting sites at NC A&T and UNC Greensboro have historically been used only in presidential election years (general elections since 2004 at A&T and 2012 at UNCG; some presidential primaries since 2020). They have never been used for midterm elections, including under previous Democratic-majority boards (e.g., the unanimous 2022 midterm plan had none).\u2060Wfae\n\nWhat happened in 2025\u20132026\nAfter the board shifted to a 3\u20132 Republican majority (with Republican chair Eugene Lester), the majority declined to add the campus sites for the 2026 midterm primary and general election. Democrats on the board pushed to include them; the Republican majority (sometimes joined by one Democrat on compromise plans) rejected pure on-campus locations.\u2060Ncnewsline\n\nThe board instead approved plans with more total sites than recent midterms (10 for the primary vs. 8 historically; 17 for the general), \n\nThey spin everything into a topic of oppression.", "author": "GenWashington", "created": 1792226546522, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "They spin everything into a topic of oppression: Guilford County NC Board of Elections currently has a Republican majority (3\u20132), with a Republican chair.\nThey expanded poll locations and closed special on campus polls. What did the left do?", "last_comment_created": 1792226546522, "content": "<p>Campus early-voting sites at NC A&amp;T and UNC Greensboro have historically been used only in presidential election years (general elections since 2004 at A&amp;T and 2012 at UNCG; some presidential primaries since 2020). They have never been used for midterm elections, including under previous Democratic-majority boards (e.g., the unanimous 2022 midterm plan had none).\u2060Wfae</p>\n<p>What happened in 2025\u20132026\nAfter the board shifted to a 3\u20132 Republican majority (with Republican chair Eugene Lester), the majority declined to add the campus sites for the 2026 midterm primary and general election. Democrats on the board pushed to include them; the Republican majority (sometimes joined by one Democrat on compromise plans) rejected pure on-campus locations.\u2060Ncnewsline</p>\n<p>The board instead approved plans with more total sites than recent midterms (10 for the primary vs. 8 historically; 17 for the general),</p>\n<p>They spin everything into a topic of oppression.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 21, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "\ud83d\uded1\u00a0\u00a0Corrupt Commies\u00a0\u00a0\ud83d\uded1", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2111225700497957140", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVf24w0l", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 99, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8889937, "raw_content": "", "author": "PiratePatriotParrot", "created": 1792196171030, "profile_pictu